cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use bwebs, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "bwebs: Bayesian Food Webs from Compiled Trophic Interactions"
version: 0.3.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/STABLE-uv/bwebs"
authors:
  - family-names: "Amador Crespo"
    given-names: "Pablo"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-3793-8794"
  - family-names: "Rico"
    given-names: "Andreu"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1820-4218"
abstract: >-
  R package that infers the potential trophic links among the taxa of a
  community from compilations of published interactions (the registry of
  Gray et al. 2015, Global Biotic Interactions and the freshwater food webs
  of GATEWAy), estimates with a Bayesian hierarchical model how often links
  inferred with each class of taxonomic evidence are observed in independent
  food webs, gives the pairs without an inferred link a probability that
  decays with the taxonomic distance of their closest records, lowers the
  probability of predation between taxa of implausible body sizes, samples
  plausible food webs from those probabilities for every sample of an
  abundance or biomass table and summarises their topological indicators
  with credible intervals.
keywords:
  - R
  - food webs
  - ecological networks
  - trophic interactions
  - metaweb
  - Bayesian calibration
  - freshwater ecology
